      ],
      "finding": "Section name is a borrowed pointer, explicitly not copied. Hash lookup copy=false; newsect->name=name. Caller must keep backing name bytes alive through all BFD access, including close writing/cleanup. BFD does not own/free caller name allocation."
    },
    {
      "function": "bfd_close",
      "provider": "opncls.c",
      "lines": [
        890,
        892,
        893,
        895
      ],
      "finding": "Saves write result then evaluates bfd_close_all_done(abfd) as the LEFT operand of && ret. Thus it calls all_done even if writing failed; false does not mean handle remains valid."
    },
    {
      "function": "bfd_close_all_done",
      "provider": "opncls.c",
      "lines": [
        920,
        922,
        924,
        926,
        932,
        933,
        934,
        936
      ],
      "finding": "Calls target close_and_cleanup; invokes iovec bclose only when target cleanup succeeded; unconditionally calls _bfd_delete_bfd and frees global error buffer, even when returning false. A cleanup failure may skip bclose, but handle is still freed. No retry on same handle is valid."
    },
