  "repair_implications": [
    "Maintain owned section name storage until one terminal bfd_close or bfd_close_all_done returns, then free caller storage exactly once.",
    "Normal success uses bfd_close exactly once; its return value controls success/failure reporting, never a second close.",
    "For earlier conversion/write errors, bfd_close_all_done once can destroy the live handle without completing pending writes. Never call it after bfd_close, including false.",
    "Mark handle consumed before/at terminal call so cleanup logic cannot call twice; preserve original failure before cleanup may change BFD error state."
  ],
  "remaining_exact_provider_gap": [
    "PINNED-ABI /usr/lib64/libbfd.so is a382-byte GNU ld linker script, not ELF. It selects /usr/lib64/libbfd.a plus libsframe.a/liberty/z/dl. Header and script match official sameNEVRA exactly, but selected SDK libbfd.a bytes are not recorded by PINNED-ABI and have NOT been compared to extracted official static archive. Therefore selected actual linked implementation proof remains OPEN; this is source/package evidence and does not assert actual SDK/provider identity or native acceptance."
  ],
